                "entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                "word": "mangeable",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3d07566d-4849-4eaa-835f-1cfac1153e13",
                        "entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "mangeables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc737610-8d32-3ee8-83cc-3958bcf8214d",
                        "entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Comestible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1068eaac-0315-40f1-9d7a-0323b96bf5a0",
                                "sense_id": "cc737610-8d32-3ee8-83cc-3958bcf8214d",
                                "text": "Le fruit le plus exquis de l'Orient et peut être du monde, est le mangoustan (garcinia mangostana). […]; il est petit et sphérique : une écorce brune, dure à l'extérieur, plus douce et moins foncée intérieurement, recouvre une pulpe blanche et transparente comme la neige : cette pulpe est la seule partie mangeable du fruit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74311c92-8f3a-4531-a13e-cc3d972428e8",
                                "sense_id": "cc737610-8d32-3ee8-83cc-3958bcf8214d",
                                "text": "Quand les Égyptiens et les Incas les éliminaient par trempage prolonger dans l'eau, ils ne le faisaient pas forcément dans l'intention de les rendre moins toxiques, mais d'abord de les rendre mangeables."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b6e1965-23fd-325a-b423-529c0ccd3eb7",
                        "entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui peut se manger sans dégoût."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0ab850c-0c8b-448d-9e02-60a28057bf73",
                                "sense_id": "4b6e1965-23fd-325a-b423-529c0ccd3eb7",
                                "text": "Si l'on blanchit trop ce chou , il se réduira en bouillie en le cuisant pour la table : et s'il ne l'est pas suffisamment, on ne pourra le cuire assez pour le rendre mangeable; l'expérience seule apprend le point juste."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ca2f563-8860-41bb-8a9b-34be21dffcc1",
                                "sense_id": "4b6e1965-23fd-325a-b423-529c0ccd3eb7",
                                "text": "Elle cuisinait les viandes à la poêle, dans un bruit déchirant, avec des odeurs empoisonnées ; et rien de ce qu’elle servait n’était mangeable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ef4282c-7ba9-403a-b97c-623542d1c802",
                                "sense_id": "4b6e1965-23fd-325a-b423-529c0ccd3eb7",
                                "text": "La salade bulgare était un peu plus sophistiquée qu'ailleurs et l'agneau mangeable. En tout cas, Mara était ravie comme une enfant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68b1b750-47c4-46c0-8157-6792a6aeec22",
                                "sense_id": "4b6e1965-23fd-325a-b423-529c0ccd3eb7",
                                "text": "En somme, sans le sel, le pain n'est pas mangeable et si le pain n'est pas mangeable, rien n'est mangeable, et si rien n'est mangeable, la vie ne se préserve pas."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8d2081e8-0e2b-4e06-93c4-bad8e112ffb2",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                        "target_lang_word": "eatable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eatable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57f750f1-1636-31c7-b0b1-38c1171f10bf",
                                        "entry_id": "6ddb7dce-b58a-3fb6-96e5-15dca17d2274",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be eaten; edible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cba075c8-2fec-4f1b-9fcd-639f3ce4e1f9",
                                                "sense_id": "57f750f1-1636-31c7-b0b1-38c1171f10bf",
                                                "text": "The contents of the pan began to boil, and he turned to plunge his hand into the bowl; I conjectured that this preparation was probably for our supper, and, being hungry, I resolved it should be eatable;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "709fb82c-4b0e-4032-ab0f-0dc63a9848c5",
                                                "sense_id": "57f750f1-1636-31c7-b0b1-38c1171f10bf",
                                                "text": "When the seeds are larger, softer, and more eatable, they are protected by an excessively hard and stony covering, as in the plum and peach tribe ; or they are enclosed in a tough horny core, as with crabs and apples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80803beb-0934-493c-9ac4-c9a139503551",
                                                "sense_id": "57f750f1-1636-31c7-b0b1-38c1171f10bf",
                                                "text": "Their diet includes practically everything eatable they can capture or kill."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "eatable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                        "entry_id": "0c943cb5-18a8-35be-852a-9a94fb7551d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything edible; food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b1c4e26-3e4b-4855-a33e-067fac58dc9d",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "The Excise which is laid very high throughout all Sicily, especially upon all eatables and wearing apparel is usually there […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a728a1c6-495f-4851-a877-e138849f1da0",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "Ecod, your worship, I never have courage till I see the eatables and drinkables brought upo’ the table, and then I’m as bauld as a lion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45264656-22e8-4f82-869d-0c8ff1462ae0",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "[…] the ground […] was already being occupied by the “cheap Jacks,” with their green-covered carts and marvellous assortment of wares; and the booths of more legitimate small traders, with their tempting arrays of fairings and eatables; and penny peep-shows and other shows, containing pink-eyed ladies, and dwarfs, and boa-constrictors, and wild Indians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "725c683e-28dc-4172-a266-2bfacd539fe7",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "Someplace in the Hegdehaugen area I stopped outside a grocer's where some food was displayed in the window. A cat lay asleep beside a round loaf of white bread, and just behind it was a bowl of lard and several jars of oats. I stood eyeing these eatables a while, but since I didn't have anything to buy with I turned away from them and continued my tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b10f8303-25e7-4fa2-82a9-14a166a19d84",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "“You’ll be using the best tea-set, of course, Marilla,” she said. “Can I fix up the table with ferns and wild roses?”\n“I think that’s all nonsense,” sniffed Marilla. “In my opinion it’s the eatables that matter and not flummery decorations.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d17c3a3e-f07b-4c18-b363-539c17fb5404",
                                                "sense_id": "bdf9c1cb-3d4e-3322-a485-9f9cc3af4701",
                                                "text": "The presence of a large number of people ensured that vendors selling eatables made brisk business."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "21374254-e268-49f6-a634-79ce28e4f584",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e292ec4-5055-3993-a152-c6b9dcc6ebe3",
                        "target_lang_word": "edible",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "edible",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77edab93-514e-33f3-9f8b-d4d46f817542",
                                        "entry_id": "91c5daf1-f135-32f9-9035-10876c07b1fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being eaten without harm; suitable for consumption; innocuous to humans."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e839e72e-52cc-499d-b84d-7d162d4cc357",
                                                "sense_id": "77edab93-514e-33f3-9f8b-d4d46f817542",
                                                "text": "edible fruit"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bee0e29-99a7-3398-83a5-1c94fe1e43df",
                                        "entry_id": "91c5daf1-f135-32f9-9035-10876c07b1fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Capable of being eaten without disgust or disrelish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "123df4df-fcd7-4b14-9d5e-6279c00395d0",
                                                "sense_id": "5bee0e29-99a7-3398-83a5-1c94fe1e43df",
                                                "text": "Although stale, the bread was edible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a69d7280-e885-410e-98ee-a27134a112f4",
                                                "sense_id": "5bee0e29-99a7-3398-83a5-1c94fe1e43df",
                                                "text": "However, rather than try to place the Viceroy in a rigid, all-or-none category which implies more than the data show, the Viceroy is here considered more edible than its model, the Monarch, but initially less edible (except to C-2) than the non-mimetic butterflies used in these experiments."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b6e8398-83aa-4e2a-9245-7d49697e5aaa",
                                                "sense_id": "5bee0e29-99a7-3398-83a5-1c94fe1e43df",
                                                "text": "Recently germinated seeds are often even more nutritious from the point of view of humans because the stored chemicals are often transformed into more edible and palatable substances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edae1523-000c-42c4-b0ce-2ac7f46b4724",
                                                "sense_id": "5bee0e29-99a7-3398-83a5-1c94fe1e43df",
                                                "text": "This gets to the heart of the matter because, in the parthenogenic state, the fruits are more edible (though there are also apparently advantages to pollinated figs, which may be bigger and stronger) and the trees more productive from the human's point of view."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb356a43-e6f8-36b7-89a0-4851c22e32d7",
                                        "entry_id": "91c5daf1-f135-32f9-9035-10876c07b1fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In which edible plants are grown for human consumption."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c49b6637-9086-4aa6-9601-0a74010988dd",
                                                "sense_id": "cb356a43-e6f8-36b7-89a0-4851c22e32d7",
                                                "text": "Gardens do not contain flowers and ornamental plants, but edible plants. Although edible, these gardens are equally valued for their aesthetic qualities. It is women who collect from edible gardens, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99c2029-d087-4d43-b2ad-3735e6f4dee7",
                                                "sense_id": "cb356a43-e6f8-36b7-89a0-4851c22e32d7",
                                                "text": "To get started, how about creating an edible window box? Sowed in the spring, salad seeds like radish, lettuce and spring onion will germinate so quickly that you'll be harvesting a crop in a month or two."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
